Here's a C version:

```c
int remove_duplicates(const int *items, int n, int *out) {
    int m = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        int dup = 0;
        for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {
            if (out[j] == items[i]) { dup = 1; break; }
        }
        if (!dup) out[m++] = items[i];
    }
    return m;
}
```

Track the values already seen in a set and keep only the first appearance of each. C has no built-in array length or string type, so the length is passed explicitly or the string is NUL-terminated.

**Complexity:** O(n) time, O(n) space.

For example, `remove_duplicates([3, 1, 3, 2, 1, 4])` gives `3 1 2 4`.

