Two strings are anagrams if they use exactly the same letters the same number of times. Count the letters of one and cancel them with the other. The type annotations are erased at runtime; they just let the compiler catch mistakes like passing a string where a number is expected.

**Complexity:** O(n) time with counting, O(1) extra space for a fixed alphabet (sorting is O(n log n)).

