```python
class Queue:
    def __init__(self):
        self._in, self._out = [], []

    def enqueue(self, x):
        self._in.append(x)

    def dequeue(self):
        if not self._out:
            while self._in:
                self._out.append(self._in.pop())
        if not self._out:
            raise IndexError("dequeue from empty queue")
        return self._out.pop()
```

Items are pushed onto the input stack; when the output stack is empty everything is reversed over into it, which restores first-in-first-out order. Each item moves at most once, so operations are O(1) amortised.

